;; The files of the tree check (bin/repr-c parse-check; doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: C3") whose dumps are
;; known to differ from cc's, by corpus, each with its class (the classes below); a file the token check's
;; known file lists at :pp (test/repr/c/pp-check-known.edn) is known here too. Written by bin/repr-c
;; parse-check --record, the classes kept. Read with the Clojure reader.
{:classes
 {:pp-errors "the trees equal, the errors not: the preprocessor's errors, where the port follows gcc (#if's binary constants and wb suffixes, __has_c_attribute's answers in #error tests, #elifdef, a missing #embed resource) and cc reports another or none"
  :invalid-paste "a ## that does not make one token (6.10.5.3, a mutant's): cc joins the texts, the port keeps the two tokens and reports gcc's error (the token check's class)"
  :trigraphs "phase 1's trigraphs, which cc does not read and gcc does at -std=c89 to c17 and with -trigraphs: the port follows gcc (CS50 (a))"
  :ucn-identifier "universal character names in identifiers, which cc lexes as a backslash and an identifier and gcc as one identifier: the port follows gcc (CS50 (a))"
  :pp-known "the preprocessed stream is known to differ from cc's (test/repr/c/pp-check-known.edn, its class there: the reference's tokens where cc is wrong), and the tree with it"
  :eval-depth "the parse recurses deeper than the evaluator's 10,000 interpreted calls (Compiler's MAX_DEPTH): cc's Go stack grows to 1 GB, the port evaluated on the tools' host gives the evaluator's StackOverflowError, a panic (CS60)"}
 :parse
 {:gcc-bitint
  {"gcc.dg/bitint-2.c" {:class :pp-errors}
   "gcc.dg/bitint-22.c" {:class :pp-errors}
   "gcc.dg/bitint-23.c" {:class :pp-errors}
